  {
    "objectID": "index.html",
    "href": "index.html",
    "title": "Teaching Gemma to Code",
    "section": "",
    "text": "Why this handbook\nMy advisor suggested I enter the Gemma 4 Developer Agent competition. The task: build an agent on Gemma 4 that fixes real GitHub issues, scored by whether the fix passes that issue’s tests.\nI use coding agents every day, but I wanted to know how one works inside, and to measure it instead of guessing. So I’m writing down what I learn, chapter by chapter, with the code and the scores next to it.\nEvery number in this handbook comes from a run I can point to in the experiment log. When something didn’t work, I say so.",
    "crumbs": [
      "Why this handbook"
    ]
  },
